----------
scriptunit-fragment
----------

let a = 1000

----------
scriptunit-fragment
----------

var b = 125

----------
scriptunit-fragment
----------

let c = a /! b

----------
scriptunit-fragment
----------

set b = b * 2

----------
expect all four units are entered
----------

| unit | uses | this step | because | holds after |
|------|------|-----------|---------|-------------|
| 1 | - | compiles, runs | new | `a` = 1000 |
| 2 | - | compiles, runs | new | `b` = 250 |
| 3 | reads `a` (1), reads `b` (2) | compiles, runs | new | `c` = 8 |
| 4 | updates `b` (2) | compiles, runs | new | - |

----------
scriptunit-edit 3
----------

let c = (a /! b) * 2

----------
expect unit 3 is edited
----------

| unit | uses | this step | because | holds after |
|------|------|-----------|---------|-------------|
| 1 | - | untouched | nothing changed `a` | `a` = 1000 |
| 2 | - | reruns | rewind: unit 3 reads `b`, which unit 4 updated after it | `b` = 250 |
| 3 | reads `a` (1), reads `b` (2) | recompiles, runs | edited | `c` = 16 |
| 4 | updates `b` (2) | reruns | replay: updates `b` from unit 2, which reran | - |
